    "https://uni.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UNI/job/Main-Campus/Temporary-Athletic-Trainer_JR1469": {
      "title": "Temporary Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-04\nPart time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and from the Navigation Side Bar, go to Personal then UNI Internal Careers. Full Consideration Date: 11/06/2026 Job Description: Summary: Provides on-site athletic training coverage for athletic facility rental events on a temporary, as-needed basis. Delivers first aid, injury assessment, emergency care, and other athletic training services to support the health and safety of event participants. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree; at least five years of athletic training experience in the field post certification; certification by the National Athletic Trainers’ Association Board of Certification (NATABOC); and Athletic Training Licensure (or eligibility for licensure) in the State of Iowa; strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills; and ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented environment. Preferred Qualifications: NCAA Division I experience; and experience with manual therapy rehabilitation techniques. Position Details: Job Category: Professional and Scientific Type of Position: Temp Schedule: Hours will vary, as this position provides coverage for athletic facility rental events as needed. Application Instructions: All application materials must be submitted by November 6, 2026, to be considered for this position. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following materials must be attached when applying: 1) Resume 2) Cover Letter You will be presented with the opportunity to attach multiple documents when completing the application. Before submitting your online job application, ensure that ALL required materials listed above have been uploaded. Once your job application has been submitted, you cannot make changes. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email careers