    "https://uni.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UNI/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Adjunct-Professor---Mathematics_JR1465-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Adjunct Professor - Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nPart time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and type “Find Jobs” in the search bar to view and apply for open positions. Full Consideration Date: 11/16/2026 Job Description: The University of Northern Iowa's Department of Mathematics is seeking applications for an Assistant Adjunct Professor position, starting in January 2027. This position will teach one or two sections (sections 62 & 63) of the course MATH 2204: Mathematics Reasoning for Elementary Teachers II. The two sections are offered through the University of Northern Iowa Online & Distance Education. This position is eligible to be performed remotely within the state of Iowa. Employees who elect remote work must comply with the requirements of our remote work policy and agreement. Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Mathematics Education or an equivalent graduate degree required. Preferred Qualifications: Online teaching experience at the college level preferred. For more information, please contact Douglas Mupasiri, Search Committee Chair, at 319-273-2631 or e-mail at douglas.mupasiri@uni.edu . Pre-employment background checks required. Position Details: Job Category:  Faculty Type of Position:  Temporary Service Schedule:  Spring semester Application Instructions:  All application materials must be submitted before 11/16/2026 to be considered for this position. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following materials must be attached when applying: 1) Curriculum Vitae 2) Cover Letter You will have the opportunity to attach multiple documents when completing the application. Before submitting your online job application, ensure that ALL required materials listed above have been uploaded. Once your job application has been submitted, you cannot make changes. If you have questions regarding this application proce