      "title": "Secretary II - Educational Talent Search",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and type “Find Jobs” in the search bar to view and apply for open positions. Full Consideration Date: 11/4/2026 Job Description: Under general supervision, performs general secretarial duties for the Educational Talent Search (ETS) Cedar Rapids program; answers telephone to provide assistance to individuals interested in the program; supervises clerical student employees; composes and types correspondence; compiles materials for financial reports and records; maintains student and personnel records; arranges meetings and appointments; maintains inventory of office supplies and equipment; and performs other related duties as requested. Minimum Eligibility Requirements: Any combination of related clerical office experience, related undergraduate education and/or post high school clerical training that is the equivalent to two years of full-time employment and includes the use of word processing. Position Details: Job Category: Merit Type of Position: Regular Service Schedule: Calendar Year Work Schedule: 20 hours per week. Exact schedule falling within office hours of Monday - Friday, 8:00 am to 4:30 pm will be discussed. Pay Gade: 8 Starting Hourly Rate: $19.09 Location: UNI-CUE; 800 Sycamore Street, Waterloo IA Application Instructions: All application materials received by November 4, 2026, will be given full consideration. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following materials are required and must be attached when applying: 1) Resume 2) Cover Letter You will have the opportunity to attach multiple documents when completing the application. Before submitting your online job application, ensure that ALL required materials listed above have been uploaded. Once your job application has been submitted, you cannot make changes. If you h