    "https://uni.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UNI/job/Main-Campus/Temporary---Dining-Service-Assistant_JR1343": {
      "title": "Temporary - Dining Service Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\nPart time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and type “Find Jobs” in the search bar to view and apply for open positions. Full Consideration Date: Applications are being continuously accepted. Job Description: Join the team making it happen! Serving up the #1 college food in Iowa, UNI Dining Services has temporary Dining Service Assistant positions open. Assists with basic food preparation tasks; cleans and maintains kitchen and dining room areas; washes and distributes dishes; and serves guests. These are intermittent call-in positions with varying work schedule based on need. Temporary positions are limited to a maximum of 1040 hours per fiscal year. Hourly rate is $12.50. Minimum Eligibility Requirements: Ability to read, write and follow instructions. Notice to Applicants: Hiring timelines vary based on staffing needs and position availability. Interviews are conducted on an as-needed basis to fill open roles. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. A resume and cover letter are not required for this position but can be attached when applying. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email careers-support@uni.edu or call 319-273-2422. Iowa's cost of living is among the lowest in the nation and the Common Sense Institute ranks Iowa #1 for paycheck stretch. UNI enhances this advantage with an excellent benefits package for eligible non-temporary positions. Visit our Compensation Tools page to explore your estimated total compensation, compare Waterloo-Cedar Falls cost of living to other major cities or review the paycheck stretch ranking details. Learn more about the Cedar Valley at https://livethevalley.com/ . If you would like general assistance with the application process or an accommodation due to a disability, please contact Human Resource Services at hrs-employment@uni.edu or call (319) 273-2422. All offers of employment are contingent upon a background check that includes a review of conviction history.  A conviction does not automatically preclude University employment.  Rather, the University considers conviction information on a case-by-case basis and assesses the nature of the offense, the circumstances surrounding it, the proximity in time of the conviction, and its relevance to the position. UNI is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any status protected by federal and/or state law. Campus Security & Crime Statistics, in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, information on crime statistics for recent years, Public Safety personnel and programs, building access, reporting crimes, safety suggestions, and policies, programs, and services regarding alcohol, drugs, and sexual abuse, is available in the UNI Annual Security and Fire Report. A paper copy is available from the Department of Public Safety, 030 Gilchrist Hall, University of Northern Iowa, Cedar Falls, IA 50614. Department of Public Safety, 030 Gilchrist Hall, University of Northern Iowa, Cedar Falls, IA 50614. Privacy Statement | Equal Opportunity and Non-Discrimination Statement | Federal EEO Rights | E-Verify | Policies and Procedures | Tobacco Free Campus"
    },
    "https://uni.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UNI/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice---Construction-Management_JR1471": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice - Construction Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-09\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and from the Navigation Side Bar, go to Personal then UNI Internal Careers. Full Consideration Date: 12/11/2026 Job Description: The University of Northern Iowa’s Department of Construction Management seeks applications for a full-time Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice position, starting in January 2027. This is a full-time, nine-month, 2.5-year term position (non-tenure track). The successful candidate will have an interest and expertise in teaching various construction management courses. Course topics include: construction project management, construction estimating, preconstruction management, mechanical/electrical construction, heavy construction operations (civil construction), construction planning & scheduling, and structural building systems for non-engineers. Courses will be taught in person at the University’s campus in Cedar Falls, IA. This successful candidate shall be expected to teach four classes and perform university service. The breakdown of these duties shall be 80% teaching and 20% service. Service shall include department committees, student clubs and organizations, etc. The Department of Construction Management consists of 2 full-time and 4 adjunct faculty members serving 200 undergraduate students. The department serves the construction industry with the only construction management program in the state. The department is housed in a recently upgraded, state-of-the-art facility with over 75,000 SF of space. The department has strong ties to community college construction programs and a long history of engagement with the construction industry, with a very active and financially generous advisory board. This position affords the successful candidate a unique opportunity for faculty leadership due to recent retirements. Education Requirements : B achelor's degree from an accredited university in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, Architecture, or a related field required.  Required Qualifications : Enthusiasm for and commitment to engaged/applied learning and teaching; at least 10 years of United States construction industry experience; effective organizational, communication and interpersonal skills; and w illingness to develop partnerships with local, regional and national construction-related businesses and organizations required.  Preferred Qualifications : Master's or terminal degree in Construction Engineering, Construction Management, Civil Engineering or related field; p rofessional certification, such as the Certified Professional Constructor (CPC), Designated Design Build Professional, (DBIA), Professional Engineering (PE), Project Management (PMP), Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED), or licensed Architect; experience developing partnerships with local, regional and national construction-related businesses and organizations; and p revious teaching experience at the university or community college level preferred.  Position Details: Job Category: Faculty Type of Position: Term Service Schedule: Academic Year For more information, please contact Randy Sharp, Search Committee Chair, at randy.sharp@uni.edu . Pre-employment background checks required.   Applications Instructions: All application materials received by December 11, 2026, will be given full consideration. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following materials must be attached when applying: 1) Curriculum Vita 2) Cover letter addressing qualifications You will have the opportunity to attach multiple documents when completing the application. Before submitting your online job application, ensure that ALL required materials listed above have been uploaded. Once your job application has been submitted, you cannot make changes. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email careers-support@uni.edu or call 319-273-2422 and press option 2 for applicant support. Iowa's cost of living is among the lowest in the nation and the Common Sense Institute ranks Iowa #1 for paycheck stretch. UNI enhances this advantage with an excellent benefits package for eligible non-temporary positions. Visit our Compensation Tools page to explore your estimated total compensation, compare Waterloo-Cedar Falls cost of living to other major cities or review the paycheck stretch ranking details. Learn more about the Cedar Valley at https://livethevalley.com/ . If you would like general assistance with the application process or an accommodation due to a disability, please contact Human Resource Services at hrs-employment@uni.edu or call (319) 273-2422. All offers of employment are contingent upon a background check that includes a review of conviction history.  A conviction does not automatically preclude University employment.  Rather, the University considers conviction information on a case-by-case basis and assesses the nature of the offense, the circumstances surrounding it, the proximity in time of the conviction, and its relevance to the position. UNI is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any status protected by federal and/or state law. Campus Security & Crime Statistics, in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, information on crime statistics for recent years, Public Safety personnel and programs, building access, reporting crimes, safety suggestions, and policies, programs, and services regarding alcohol, drugs, and sexual abuse, is available in the UNI Annual Security and Fire Report. A paper copy is available from the Department of Public Safety, 030 Gilchrist Hall, University of Northern Iowa, Cedar Falls, IA 50614. Department of Public Safety, 030 Gilchrist Hall, University of Northern Iowa, Cedar Falls, IA 50614. Privacy Statement | Equal Opportunity and Non-Discrimination Statement | Federal EEO Rights | E-Verify | Policies and Procedures | Tobacco Free Campus"
    },
    "https://uni.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UNI/job/Main-Campus/Child-Development-Specialist---Child-Development-Center_JR1476": {
      "title": "Child Development Specialist - Child Development Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-10\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and from the Navigation Side Bar, go to Personal then UNI Internal Careers. Full Consideration Date: 11/29/2026 Job Description: Join the UNI Child Development Center, where you'll make a lasting impact on young learners in a nurturing, nationally accredited early childhood environment. Plus, UNI offers eligible employees an excellent benefits package and free professional development opportunities specific to these positions. Based on qualifications, the successful candidate will be hired at one of two professional levels: Assistant Child Development Specialist or Child Development Specialist . This position will rotate classrooms as needed and support early care and education activities. Skills are taught and learned through small- and large-group time using play-based learning strategies. The curriculum matches the developmental level of the children in each classroom and includes group experiences, short-term projects, fine- and gross-motor activities, and both child- and teacher-directed experiences. Primary Function: Assistant Child Development Specialist : Plans and implements a developmentally appropriate curriculum focused on meeting the needs of the individual child, and of small and large groups of children of varying ages and interests; ensures curriculum meets the needs of all learners and various subgroups of students, such as students with dual languages and students with disabilities; engages with parents daily, initiating written and/or face-to-face communication; conducts parent-teacher conferences each semester and is available to meet with families as needed; and responsible for training and supervision of college student assistants. Child Development Specialist : Plans and implements a developmentally appropriate curriculum focused on meeting the needs of the individual child, and of small and large groups of children of varying ages and interests; ensures curriculum meets the needs of all learners and various subgroups of students, such as students with dual languages and students with disabilities; writes developmental summaries of children based on assessment information; engages with parents daily, initiating written and/or face-to-face communication; conducts parent-teacher conferences each semester and is available to meet with families as needed; responsible for supervision and documentation of field experience student activities in the Child Development Center; consults with faculty in regard to college students’ performance; and responsible for training and supervision of college student assistants. Qualifications: Assistant Child Development Specialist :  Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree plus current CPR, First Aid, Mandatory Reporter, Universal Precautions (OSHA), and Essential Child Care Training certifications or ability to acquire certification within 90 days of hire. Occasional work outside of normal hours will be necessary. Preferred Qualifications: Childcare experience. Student experience will be considered. Child Development Specialist : Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in early childhood, elementary education or related field; teaching license or 36 hours of higher education credits completed in early childhood education, child development, elementary education, or early childhood special education, or progress toward 36 credit hour started upon hire and completed within four years of hire; and current CPR/First Aid, Mandatory Reporter, Universal Precautions (OSHA), and Essentials Child Care Training certifications or ability to obtain certifications within 90 days of hire. Occasional work outside of normal hours will be necessary. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in early childhood education or related field and childcare experience. Student experience will be considered. Fall 2026 graduates will be considered. Degree must be conferred prior to start date. Position Details: Job Category: Professional and Scientific Type of Position: Term Service Schedule: Calendar Year Application Instructions: All application materials received by November 29, 2026, will be given full consideration. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following materials must be attached when applying: 1) Resume 2) Cover Letter You will have the opportunity to attach multiple documents when completing the application. Before submitting your online job application, ensure that ALL required materials listed above have been uploaded. Once your job application has been submitted, you cannot make changes. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email careers-support@uni.edu or call 319-273-2422. Compensation: The pay grade and salary will be determined by the position level into which the individual is hired. Below are the pay grades and starting salary range for each level: Assistant Child Development Specialist; pay grade 116; $33,800 to Commensurate Child Development Specialist; pay grade 117; $40,000 to Commensurate Iowa's cost of living is among the lowest in the nation and the Common Sense Institute ranks Iowa #1 for paycheck stretch. UNI enhances this advantage with an excellent benefits package for eligible non-temporary positions. Visit our Compensation Tools page to explore your estimated total compensation, compare Waterloo-Cedar Falls cost of living to other major cities or review the paycheck stretch ranking details. Learn more about the Cedar Valley at https://livethevalley.com/ . If you would like general assistance with the application process or an accommodation due to a disability, please contact Human Resource Services at hrs-employment@uni.edu or call (319) 273-2422. All offers of employment are contingent upon a background check that includes a review of conviction history.  A conviction does not automatically preclude University employment.  Rather, the University considers conviction information on a case-by-case basis and assesses the nature of the offense, the circumstances surrounding it, the proximity in time of the conviction, and its relevance to the position. UNI is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any status protected by federal and/or state law. Campus Security & Crime Statistics, in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, information on crime statistics for recent years, Public Safety personnel and programs, building access, reporting crimes, safety suggestions, and policies, programs, and services regarding alcohol, drugs, and sexual abuse, is available in the UNI Annual Security and Fire Report. A paper copy is available from the Department of Public Safety, 030 Gilchrist Hall, University of Northern Iowa, Cedar Falls, IA 50614. Department of Public Safety, 030 Gilchrist Hall, University of Northern Iowa, Cedar Falls, IA 50614. Privacy Statement | Equal Opportunity and Non-Discrimination Statement | Federal EEO Rights | E-Verify | Policies and Procedures | Tobacco Free Campus"
